  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "119",
  "quote": "A landlord who is lawfully entitled to increase the rent charged to a tenant for a rental unit may do so only if at least 12 months have elapsed",
  "reason": "Section 119(1) prohibits a landlord from increasing the rent unless at least 12 months have passed since the last rent increase or the start of the tenancy. Because the clause allows rent increases every six months, it conflicts with the Act and is void under section 4(1)."
}

